@startuml component-digitalizer-target
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: this repository shrinks to portal + orchestration + lab; the heavy
'       stages run as catalog-free "standalone" Celery tasks: new tasks in the
'       existing service repositories (same core code as their catalog tasks)
'       plus two new repositories (scan, render). The orchestrator sends each
'       command with a Celery link/link_error callback to its own queue, reads
'       the worker's outcome file, and sends the next stage. Publishing to the
'       catalog is optional; the catalog's own pipeline runs after it.
' Kind: UML component diagram, specification level, proposal. Scope: components,
'       the contract between them and the shared services they reuse. Omitted:
'       telemetry wiring (every component exports OTLP), config loading, CI.
' Source: this repo docs/design/studio-spec.md, studio/workers/stages/
'         {orchestrate,gate}.py, directory listings of stages/, pipeline/steps/,
'         studio/adapters/, vlm_service/ (2026-11-16); evilflowers-worker README,
'         docs/architecture.md, runtime.py, outcome.py, settings.py @ 8fc9c20;
'         READMEs of evilflowers-{analyzer,image,equation,text,ocr}-service,
'         analyzer develop layout.py, equation develop latex.py, ocr-service
'         processing.py (2026-11-16); Celery 5.7 docs canvas/calling/routing/
'         redis (link, link_error, chords need a backend, priorities);
'         knowledge notes Extraction-Pipeline (2026-11-14), OCR-Service,
'         Shared-Inference (2026-11-15), Books-Digitalizer (2026-11-08).
' =============================================================================

title Books digitalizer, target: portal + orchestrator here,\nstandalone tasks on the shared workers (proposal, 2026-11-16)

package "**this repo**: portal · orchestration · lab" as repo {
  component "**SPA** · React\nreview · page studio" as spa
  component "**Portal API**\nFastAPI · REST · SSE\nDZI tiles" as api
  component "**Orchestrator** · Celery\njob ledger · job_done callbacks\nadmission pump · reconcile\ngate · publish" as orch <<proposed>> <<focus>>
  component "**Lab** (not deployed)\nnotebooks · experiments" as lab
}

package "**Shared state** (dev)" as state {
  component "**Redis** db 8\nbroker" as redis <<proposed>>
  component "**postgresql18**\nvia PgBouncer\ndb digitalizer" as pg <<proposed>>
  component "**Library storage**\nraw-scans ro\ndigitized rw (NFS)" as lib <<proposed>>
}

package "**Existing repos**: + standalone task, same core" as existing {
  component "**ocr-service**\n…standalone.hocr\nengines.py" as ocr <<proposed>>
  component "**analyzer-service**\n…standalone.layout\nlayout.py (Docling)" as analyzer <<proposed>>
  component "**equation-service**\n…standalone.formulas\nlatex.py + paddleocr-vl" as equation <<proposed>>
  component "**image-service**\n…standalone.figures\nfigures.py · captions.py" as image <<proposed>>
}

package "**New repos**" as fresh {
  component "**scan-service**\nevilflowers_scan.clean\nScanTailor · DocRes" as scan <<proposed>>
  component "**render-service**\nevilflowers_render.book\nMRC · PDF/A-2b · EPUB" as render <<proposed>>
}

package "**Shared inference + catalog**" as infer {
  component "**vlm**\nPaddleOCR-VL\nPOST /v1/formulas" as vlm <<proposed>>
  component "**Ollama**\nelvira-assistant\nvision · /api/chat" as ollama
  component "**Laya**\ndecision model\n(announced)" as laya <<proposed>>
  component "**EvilFlowers catalog**\n(dev) REST /api/v1\n+ its own pipeline" as catalog
}

component "**evilflowers-worker**\n(kit) runtime · outcome files\nStandaloneJob · judges" as kit

' ---- layout only ------------------------------------------------------------------
ocr -[hidden]right- analyzer
equation -[hidden]right- image
ocr -[hidden]down- equation
vlm -[hidden]right- laya
ollama -[hidden]right- catalog
vlm -[hidden]down- ollama
scan -[hidden]right- render

' ---- portal -----------------------------------------------------------------------
spa --> api : REST · SSE
api --> orch : create run
api --> pg : SQL
orch --> pg : SQL

' ---- the contract: commands out, link callbacks + outcome files back -------------------
orch -[$accent()]-> redis : <b>send_task + link</b>\n<b>job_done / job_failed</b>
redis -[$accent()]-> fresh : <b>consume</b>
fresh -[hidden]down- existing
redis --> existing : consume\n(standalone queues)
lib <.. existing : <<write>> jobs/<job>/\n+ outcome file (all six)
orch ..> lib : <<read>> outcome,\npromote output

' ---- workers use the kit ------------------------------------------------------------
fresh ..> kit : <<use>> (all six)
render -[hidden]right- kit

' ---- shared inference and optional publish -------------------------------------------
equation --> vlm : HTTP crops
image --> laya : uncertain\nregions
image --> ollama : captions
orch --> ollama : title page\n→ metadata
orch --> catalog : optional: POST entry\n+ PDF, EPUB

$legend_live_proposed()

caption The orchestrator owns state and reaches workers only through Redis: commands out, Celery link callbacks to its own\nqueue back, results as outcome files on the library storage. Existing services keep one core and gain a catalog-free task;\nonly scanning and rendering need new repositories. Solid = the code or service exists today (SPA and API: not deployed).
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · evilflowers-books-digitalizer · docs/diagrams/component-digitalizer-target.puml
@enduml
